{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfaLJ5ZGmM3CPhqXQE73f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 04 is done: Lengauer's Theorem 2 and Kirousis & Papadimitriou's Theorem 3.1 are proved in Lean, and the gate passes. `lake build` is ok, the only `sorry` is still the §24 conjecture, and pytest gives 1,272 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n\n**What is proved** (new file `lean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/PebblingGu.lean`, imported from the root). It uses only the three standard axioms, which `paper2/axiom_check.lean` now checks.\n\n- **Lengauer Theorem 2:**\n  - For every digraph and every K ≥ 0: D can be pebbled progressively with K + 1 pebbles exactly when vs(D_u) ≤ K.\n  - His statement as written holds for K ≥ 2 and fails at K = 1 on a nonempty dag with no arcs, where (D_u, 0) is not a valid VSG instance. There is a Lean proof of that failure.\n  - On any nonempty digraph, pbw(D) = vs(D_u) + 1 = pw(D_u) + 1. It also equals Z(M_D), the MOSP value of the matrix whose column v is v and its predecessors, because D_u is exactly that matrix's MOSP graph.\n- **Kirousis & Papadimitriou Theorem 3.1:**\n  - On every nonempty graph, mpb = mpbw = vs + 1 = pw + 1.\n  - Their statement mpb = ns = mpbw holds when G has an edge.\n  - Their first equality is false on edgeless nonempty graphs: mpb = mpbw = 1 but ns = 0. This is also proved in Lean.\n- **One strengthening:** Theorem 2 never uses acyclicity, so it holds for the game on any digraph, including cycles and loops. An exact search on all 66,067 digraphs with at most 4 vertices agrees.\n- **The KP proof avoids node search entirely.** Orient the graph along the reverse of an optimal layout and place black pebbles in layout order. The pebbles on the graph at each step are exactly the \"shack\" already formalised in `Narrowness.lean`. So neither LaPaugh's theorem nor any monotonicity result is needed.\n\n**Python check.** `python -m paper2.complex_check --pebbling-gu` takes about 9 s and writes `paper2/data/pebbling_gu_check.json`. It replays the proofs' constructions move by move, with zero failures:\n- Theorem 2's strategy on every layout of D_u, for every digraph up to 4 vertices and every dag on 5.\n- The black strategy on every layout of every graph up to 7 vertices, 5.4 million plays.\n\nThe check is exhaustive only up to those sizes; the Lean proofs cover all sizes. `tests/test_pebbling_check.py` has 16 new tests, including one that deletes a step of Lengauer's strategy and confirms the play becomes illegal.\n\n**Docs.**\n- `paper2/problem_transformations.md`:\n  - §1.13 extended with D_u, the black game and mpb/mpbw;\n  - new transformations (E11) and (E12);\n  - the edge cases added to (F3);\n  - both proofs, formal and then in plain English.\n- `paper2/equivalences.md`:\n  - master table row 13 for pebbling, marked as not a Table 1 row;\n  - rows 13a and 13b marked proved;\n  - new section P.9.\n\n`PROGRESS.md` is at 4/13 with the item marked `[x]`; I committed nothing. Phase A is complete. Adding pebbling to the chain figure is left to item 12, and item 05 (stating the customer search) is next."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_read_input_tokens":241508,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":226,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":859,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ad89bb0-108d-46ad-9278-059e6bd9be28","uuid":"6422e052-a8aa-40eb-8cf6-440d5fe40f9e","timestamp":"2026-09-30T21:28:14.580Z","request_id":"req_011CfaLJ58yRw2rBySQ6FqFx"}
